---
import DocsLayout from '../../components/DocsLayout.astro';
import { Code } from 'astro:components';
---

<DocsLayout title="Getting Started" section="getting-started">
  <h1>Getting Started</h1>
  <p class="lead">Fanar is a local debug receiver. Download the desktop app, install a client library, and start sending payloads in under a minute.</p>

  <h2>1. Download the app</h2>
  <p>Fanar runs a local HTTP server on <code>localhost:23517</code>. Download and open it — no account, no configuration required.</p>
  <table>
    <tr><th>Platform</th><th>Download</th></tr>
    <tr><td>macOS Apple Silicon</td><td><a href="https://github.com/fanar-app/fanar-app/releases/latest/download/fanar-macos-arm64.zip" class="text-[#a78bfa] hover:text-white transition-colors">fanar-macos-arm64.zip</a></td></tr>
    <tr><td>macOS Intel</td><td><a href="https://github.com/fanar-app/fanar-app/releases/latest/download/fanar-macos-x64.zip" class="text-[#a78bfa] hover:text-white transition-colors">fanar-macos-x64.zip</a></td></tr>
    <tr><td>Windows</td><td><a href="https://github.com/fanar-app/fanar-app/releases/latest/download/fanar-windows-x64.exe" class="text-[#a78bfa] hover:text-white transition-colors">fanar-windows-x64.exe</a></td></tr>
    <tr><td>Linux</td><td><a href="https://github.com/fanar-app/fanar-app/releases/latest/download/fanar-linux-x64" class="text-[#a78bfa] hover:text-white transition-colors">fanar-linux-x64</a></td></tr>
  </table>

  <h2>2. Install a client</h2>
  <p>Pick the library for your stack. Or skip directly to the <a href="/docs/http-api/" class="text-[#a78bfa] hover:text-white transition-colors">HTTP API</a> — any language that can POST JSON works.</p>

  <h3>Node.js / TypeScript</h3>
  <Code code={`npm install fanar`} lang="bash" theme="github-dark" />

  <h3>PHP / Laravel</h3>
  <Code code={`composer require fanar/fanar`} lang="bash" theme="github-dark" />

  <h2>3. Send your first payload</h2>
  <p>Call <code>fanar()</code> anywhere in your code. The payload appears in the desktop app instantly.</p>
  <Code code={`import fanar from 'fanar'

fanar('hello world')          // string log
fanar({ user, cart })         // object — collapsible JSON tree
fanar(new Error('oh no'))     // exception — clickable stack frames`} lang="javascript" theme="github-dark" />

  <h2>4. What appears in the app</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Every <code>fanar()</code> call streams in real time — no polling, no page refresh</li>
    <li>Objects render as an expandable JSON tree</li>
    <li>Exceptions show a full stack trace with clickable file:line links that open VS Code</li>
    <li>SQL queries show syntax highlighting, bound values, and execution time</li>
    <li>Timers show elapsed time between <code>.start()</code> and <code>.stop()</code></li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Keyboard shortcuts</h2>
  <table>
    <tr><th>Shortcut</th><th>Action</th></tr>
    <tr><td>⌘K / Ctrl+K</td><td>Clear all payloads</td></tr>
    <tr><td>⌘F / Ctrl+F</td><td>Focus search</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Space</td><td>Pause / resume live feed</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Esc</td><td>Clear search</td></tr>
    <tr><td>?</td><td>Show keyboard shortcuts</td></tr>
  </table>
</DocsLayout>
